<div class="stat-num"><div class="num">10</div><div class="label">Career Starts, All 2025</div></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>The landing spot is notable: New York just lost starting quarterback Jaxson Dart to a season-ending knee injury, and head coach John Harbaugh has confirmed Jameis Winston remains the starter for now, with McCarthy expected to serve as QB2 while he learns the offense. Harbaugh's brother Jim coached McCarthy at Michigan to a national championship — a connection the Giants hope smooths his transition.</p>
<h2 id="fall">How McCarthy Fell</h2>
<p>McCarthy missed his entire rookie season on injured reserve after a preseason meniscus injury, then started 10 games for Minnesota in 2025, going 57.6% completion with 1,632 yards, 11 touchdowns and 12 interceptions. He entered this offseason in a genuine competition for the starting job, but an ankle sprain limited him late in preseason, and Minnesota named Murray the Week 1 starter on August 11 — a decision general manager Nolan Teasley said drew "a lot of inquiries" about trading McCarthy almost immediately afterward.</p>
<h2 id="combine">The Combine Profile Teams Once Bet On</h2>
<p>McCarthy's athletic profile was always built more on mobility and processing than a blazing 40 time — he skipped both the sprint and the jump drills at the 2024 combine due to hamstring tightness, running only the throwing session and the agility drills. What he did run was notable: a 6.82-second 3-cone drill, the sixth-best time posted by any prospect at the entire 2024 combine, regardless of position, plus a 4.23-second 20-yard shuttle.</p>
