<p>That agility, paired with a 27-1 record as a college starter and a national title, was enough to make McCarthy a top-10 pick despite a limited sample size — just 713 career pass attempts across three seasons at Michigan. The bet was always that his mobility and decision-making in a structured offense would translate, and a shorter, quicker read-based scheme suits that skill set better than one demanding him to carry the offense downfield on volume alone.</p>
<div class="callout">
<strong>A Change of Scenery, Not a Change of Talent</strong>
  McCarthy's fall has been about opportunity and fit more than a collapse in his underlying skill set — his 27-1 college record and elite agility testing haven't disappeared. Whether he ever starts again for the Giants depends far more on how Dart's absence and Winston's play unfold than on anything McCarthy himself has done wrong.
</div>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Why did the Vikings trade J.J. McCarthy?</div>
<div class="faq-a">McCarthy lost the starting quarterback competition to free-agent addition Kyler Murray in August 2026, and after struggling during the preseason, the Vikings traded him to the Giants for a 2027 fifth-round pick.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Will J.J. McCarthy start for the Giants?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Not immediately. Head coach John Harbaugh confirmed Jameis Winston will remain New York's starter, with McCarthy expected to serve as the backup while he learns the offense following Jaxson Dart's season-ending injury.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Did J.J. McCarthy run the 40-yard dash at the combine?</div>
<div class="faq-a">No. McCarthy skipped the 40-yard dash and all jumping drills at the 2024 NFL Combine due to hamstring tightness, but posted a 6.82-second 3-cone drill, the sixth-best time among all prospects at that year's combine.</div>
</div>
